# We consider the "rc" form of a pre-release to be long-form for the
# "c" form, thus we normalize "rc" to "c" so we can properly compare
# them as equal. We do the same for the "alpha" and "beta" forms so
# that all of the long and short spellings of a pre-release end up in
# the same, canonical, representation.
letter = letter.lower()
if letter == "rc":
    letter = "c"
elif letter == "alpha":
    letter = "a"
elif letter == "beta":
    letter = "b"

